Expected settlement before any reveal is the sum of the die means: 8.67 (die 1) + 4.75 (die 2) + 2.5 (die 3) ≈ 15.92. Die 2 stays hidden until stage 2, so the public fair value is about 15.92.

Noise traders' valuations are centred on 15.92 with sd 4.8, and the settlement has sd about 5.7. Averaging over the three possible values of alpha (weights 1/3 each, so the effective informed weight is about 0.48), the expected profit per side is maximised at roughly 6 above or below fair. That puts the ask near 21.9 (rounded up to 22.0) and the bid near 9.9 (rounded down to 9.9). The history doesn't yet show which alpha applies, so I'm keeping the spread wide.

