Die 2 is revealed as 3. Die 1 has mean 52/6 ≈ 8.67 and die 3 has mean 10/4 = 2.5, so the public fair value is about 14.2. The earlier history (for example, no sale at bid 9.9 in round 2 when the settlement was 5) points to a low informed share, so I'm pricing mostly against noise traders.

I'm long 2, so selling is profitable above fair value and buying is profitable below it. Choosing each side to maximise expected edge against noise traders gives an ask near 17.8 and a bid near 10.6. I nudge the bid slightly lower and keep the ask at 17.8 to allow for a small informed share, since an informed buyer at the ask or seller at the bid would hurt.

