Quote 3 has no trades yet, and the two earlier no-trade quotes carry information. Card 1 = 0 leaves 21 cards for card 2 with mean 152/21 ≈ 7.24. Informed counterparties would have sold to a bid of 5.8 if card 2 were 0, 2 or 3, so their absence shifts the posterior toward higher values. Combined with the posterior over alpha, the public fair value is roughly 9.1.

Pricing against that fair value, the bid side is best near 3, where the informed sell risk (only low values) is limited. On the ask side, 15 is best because no informed buyer can take it (card 2 can't exceed 15), and only noise traders with valuations above 15 would buy.

