I'm quoting asymmetrically around that value. A bid near 6.5 and an ask near 21 each earn a small positive expected profit against noise traders after adverse selection from informed traders, averaged over the prior on alpha (mean about 0.48). The ask sits a bit further out because the sum of two cards has a heavier upper tail, which makes informed buyers more likely above 21.

