Quote 1 drew no trade, which slightly lowers the likelihood of a high informed arrival. Even so, my earlier ask of 21.3 looks too tight. An informed buyer at 21.3 would take the contract whenever the sum is 22 or more, and the expected sum given that is about 27, so the ask loses money on average. Working through the expected profit per quote over the sum distribution with alpha around 0.45 (the prior mean), the best ask sits around 27–29 and the best bid around 11–13. I'll quote near the middle of that range, which also hedges across alpha values.

