Die 2 is 11, so settlement is min(die 1, 11). The settlement distribution is 0, 1, 3, 6, 9, 11 with probability 1/8 each and 10 with probability 2/8, giving an expected value of 6.25. The public fair value is therefore 6.25, and noise traders' valuations are centred there.

Earlier quotes produced no trades, which only weakly favours a low informed share, so I use an average informed probability of about 0.5. Against that, the best ask is around 10.1 to 10.3, where noise traders still buy often enough and informed buyers rarely see value above the ask. The best bid is near 0.1, where noise sellers are rare and informed sellers almost never see value below it. Both sides have positive expected value, so I quote both.

