Fair value before any information is E[settlement] = 10 × 5 × E[p] = 10 × 5 × 0.35 = 17.5.

With alpha averaging 0.483, informed flow is expensive for a quote near fair value. An informed seller hits my bid whenever the settlement is below it, and an informed buyer lifts my ask whenever the settlement is above it. Noise traders are less costly because their valuations are centred on 17.5 with standard deviation 11. The best single quote therefore sits well away from 17.5, where informed traders rarely trade but noise traders occasionally still do. A rough expected-profit calculation over the settlement distribution gives a bid near 0 and an ask near 30.

