Posterior after flips 1-3 are all tails: P(p=0.2) ≈ 0.80, so the expected settlement is about 10 × 2 × 0.26 ≈ 5.2. The distribution is P(0) ≈ 0.56, P(10) ≈ 0.36, P(20) ≈ 0.08.

Given the uncertainty about alpha (mean about 0.48), I'm pricing the ask above fair value, where noise buyers are a profitable trade and informed buyers only hit it if the settlement is 20. For the bid, I'm keeping it at 0, where informed sellers can't hit it because the settlement is never below 0. A slightly negative bid would be marginally better, but I'm avoiding it in case negative prices aren't accepted.

