Nothing has been revealed this round, so the public fair value is the prior expectation. The coin is 0.2 or 0.5 with equal probability, so the expected heads count over 5 flips is 1.75 and the expected settlement is 17.5.

The main concern is adverse selection, since alpha could be as high as 0.9. Informed traders only trade when the settlement value is far from our quote, so a wide spread protects us. Rough expected-value estimates across the three alpha values favour bid around 3 to 5 and ask around 30 to 32. The previous quote (3 / 32) drew no trade, which is consistent with that range and carries little information, so I'll keep it.

