The coin and flips 4-5 are hidden, and flips 1-3 aren't revealed until stage 2. The prior mean is 0.35 heads, so settlement is 17.5 before any information. The counterparty's buy at 30 is informative, though: an informed buyer only buys if settlement exceeds 30, so the posterior mean rises to roughly 28.

I'm short 1 unit at 30. Given the posterior, an ask near 40 should earn a small positive expected profit from noise buyers, while still avoiding informed buyers, who only take it when settlement is 50. A bid near 10 keeps a little positive expected value, since only informed sellers at settlement 0 would sell there. Both sides are modest, but both have positive expected value under this model.

