The contract is max minus min of three dice. Before any reveal, the expected settlement is about 6.21. I computed this from the empirical CDFs of the three dice, using E[range] = Σₖ [1 − F₁F₂F₃(k) − G₁G₂G₃(k)].

Noise traders value the contract at about 6.21 ± 2.4 noise, so they trade with me when my quotes are off fair value. Informed traders (probability α, with a prior mean of about 0.48) buy whenever the settlement exceeds my ask and sell whenever it falls below my bid. Balancing the expected noise-trader profit against the informed-trader loss, using the average α and an approximate settlement standard deviation of 2.7, gives a half-spread of about 3. That puts the bid near 3.2 and the ask near 9.2.

