The settlement is max minus min of the three dice. Nothing is revealed yet, so I estimated the fair value by enumerating the dice distributions: E[max] ≈ 9.55 and E[min] ≈ 3.34, giving a fair value of about 6.2.

The main risk is adverse selection. Informed counterparties (probability alpha, prior mean about 0.48) trade whenever the true value lies outside my quotes. Noise traders have a valuation spread of only 2.4 around fair value. Balancing these, I found the expected edge per side roughly flat or slightly positive only around 3.8 from fair value (my rough estimate of the spread of the value distribution is crude). That places the ask near 10 and the bid near 2.4. This is a rough approximation, and I haven't verified the skew of the value distribution.

